   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT amending chapter 548 of the laws of 2004 amending the education law\nrelating to certain tuition waivers for police officer students of the city\nuniversity of New York, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S10523",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10523-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 548 of 2004",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10523\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act amending chapter 548 of the laws of 2004 amending the education\nlaw relating to certain tuition waivers for police officer students of\nthe city university of New York, in relation to the effectiveness there-\nof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo purpose of this bill is to extend the law that provides certain\npolice officers enrolled at CUNY with a tuition waiver for one course.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends chapter 548 of the laws of 2004 to extend\nthe law for an additional two years through July 1, 2028.\n\nSection two of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe original bill (chapter 548 of 2004) was based on a tuition waiver\nprogram sponsored by John Jay College of Criminal Justice during the\nlate 1970s through the 1980s. This bill provides a strong incentive for\npolice officers to pursue higher education by authorizing a tuition\nwavier for one course for police officer students at CUNY.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 280 of the Laws of 2022\n\nChapter 58 of the Laws of 2020(item KK of subpart b of Part XXX)\n\nChapter 67 of the Laws of 2018\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  To be determined,  \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take immediately.\n",
